  "officialHtml": "https://github.com/GraniteState/adm-rules-data/blob/1c92d82e0f03a582ca5b7a578588edf38de2318e/raw/2026-11-15/state_agencies/fire100-900.html",
  "prefLabel": "Fire 703.02 Lapse in Service",
  "recordType": "rule-section",
  "ruleText": "Fire 703.02 Lapse in Service.\n\n(a) The employment eligibility for a full-time career fire service personnel shall lapse if the employee terminates employment and is not employed as a fire service personnel within a period of 26 months after such termination.\n\n(b) If the person who has lapsed is re-employed as a full-time career fire service personnel after their employment eligibility has lapsed, the hiring authority shall follow the hiring requirements outlined in Fire 701.01 and Fire 701.02.\n\nSource #12225-B, eff 6-28-17; ss by #14172, eff 1-10-25",
  "source": "https://github.com/GraniteState/adm-rules-data/blob/1c92d82e0f03a582ca5b7a578588edf38de2318e/raw/2026-11-15/state_agencies/fire100-900.html"
